ith swappable innerHTML. One overlay, swap inner content via JS template. Simpler: two divs, toggle.\n\nBoth overlays share class .overlay.\n\nshowOverlay(id or none). hide overlay on start.\n\nStart overlay shown initially; game over overlay hidden initially.\n\nAlso while not started and animations not run, board painted.\n\nLet me write JS fully and carefully, double-checking logic.\n\nEdge case in rotate while softDrop: fine.\n\nGuard: when gameOver, loop not running (running=false). startGame sets running=true.\n\nAlso after endGame, clear softDrop=false.\n\nPreview draw after startGame: updatePreview.\n\nDraw function:\n```\nfunction draw(){\n  // empty cells\n  ctx.fillStyle = '#0b1020'; ctx.fillRect(0,0,canvas.width,canvas.height);\n  // grid\n  ctx.strokeStyle='rgba(255,255,255,0.05)';\n  for(let x=1;x<COLS;x++){ line }\n  for(let y=1;y<ROWS;y++){ line }\n  // locked\n  for y,x: if(board[y][x]) drawCell(x*CELL,y*CELL,board[y][x])\n  // ghost (only if started && !gameOver && piece)\n  if(started && !gameOver && piece){\n    let gy=piece.row; while(!collides(piece.shape,piece.col,gy+1)) gy++;\n    for cells draw ghostCell: fillStyle rgba white 0.08, stroke rgba(255,255,255,0.25)\n  }\n  // piece\n  drawCell each\n  updateHUD();\n}\n```\n\nupdateHUD: scoreEl.textContent = score; linesEl... levelEl...\n\nBoard stores color strings. Empty = null/0. Use null.\n\nDraw ghost even if gy===piece.row? fine, skip if equal? It looks odd to draw ghost under piece — skip drawing ghost if gy===piece.row.\n\ndrawCell size param: default CELL 30.\n\nPreview canvas: set width/height 148x148 in HTML attributes.\n\nScore formula: pts=[0,100,300,500,800]; score += pts[cleared]*level; then level=Math.floor(lines/10)+1 after lines+=cleared (level uses new lines). Fine.\n\nLevel → interval: Math.max(80, Math.round(800*Math.pow(0.85, level-1))).\n\nHard drop score: d*2.\n\nOK, and also keydown Enter when gameOver → startGame. Also allow clicking restart button.\n\nAlso 'r' key resta